Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 13:38:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "q6v5-pas: keep modem proxy power vote at handover
 (RF-online test)"

This reverts the local RF-online experiment, which its own commit message
described as a test: instead of releasing the AP-side proxy power vote when
the modem signals handover, it kept cx/mx/mss pinned at INT_MAX forever.

The problem it was chasing -- the modem coming up DeviceNotReady -- turned out
to have a different cause entirely (a WRQ bug in tqftpserv 1.1.1, fixed in
1.2), so the vote was never the fix. It just stayed.

The cost only became visible once qcom_stats was loaded and the system's
low-power counters could be read: with cx and mx held at maximum performance
state, aosd, cxsd and ddr can never be entered, so the SoC never reaches deep
sleep no matter what else idles. Measured over 2043 s of uptime: all three
counters at zero.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c | 12 +-----------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
index 72702ffd5..56aed30ab 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -387,23 +387,13 @@ static void qcom_pas_handover(struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5)
 {
 	struct qcom_pas *pas = container_of(q6v5, struct qcom_pas, q6v5);
 
-	/* RF-online experiment (surya modem DeviceNotReady): the modem is a PAS
-	 * subsystem at 4080000; for it, keep the AP-side proxy power vote
-	 * (cx/mx/mss at INT_MAX) instead of releasing it at handover, to test
-	 * whether the modem loses power needed to bring RF online. */
-	bool is_modem = !strcmp(dev_name(pas->dev), "4080000.remoteproc");
-
-	dev_info(pas->dev, "q6v5-pas handover (pas_id=%d, is_modem=%d): %s proxy power vote\n",
-		 pas->pas_id, is_modem, is_modem ? "KEEPING" : "releasing");
-
 	if (pas->px_supply)
 		regulator_disable(pas->px_supply);
 	if (pas->cx_supply)
 		regulator_disable(pas->cx_supply);
 	clk_disable_unprepare(pas->aggre2_clk);
 	clk_disable_unprepare(pas->xo);
-	if (!is_modem)
-		qcom_pas_pds_disable(pas, pas->proxy_pds, pas->proxy_pd_count);
+	qcom_pas_pds_disable(pas, pas->proxy_pds, pas->proxy_pd_count);
 }
 
 static int qcom_pas_stop(struct rproc *rproc)
